From 638dc1626e5ad3172874ce3ada727991b1c12026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:53:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution settings: fixes of a second independent review

- The integration by batches given by default by the execution settings is
  replaced by the integration point by point at the first setup if the
  behaviour integrators do not support it, as the computations of the
  finite elements by kernels with --execution cpu (all the processes
  decide together); a parameter given to the problem is never replaced.
- With MFEM compiled with HIP, whose kernels are not compiled in
  mfem-mgis, the finite elements and the post-processings placed on the
  GPU are refused by initialize with the options to use.
- The preconditioner None refuses the unknown parameters.
- mfem_mgis_add_behaviours_library: configuration file of TFEL searched
  next to the real bin directory of mfront, also for a TFEL installed with
  a suffix, with a message when the libraries for the GPU are not built;
  include directory relative to the current source directory; option
  NO_GPU, used by the tests when the tests on the GPU are disabled.
- Documentation: what the copy counters count (the arrays of the materials
  only, since the start of the program) with the measures on the beam,
  real limits (memory space any), no GPU rather than no device with
  --execution cpu, the environment variables ignored with --execution, the
  help of --execution and --hypre-on-host.
- ExecutionSettingsTest: a behaviour integrator without batch integration
  integrated point by point with --execution cpu (without the replacement,
  it is refused: mutation detected); solvers of MFEM with the linear
  solvers on the GPU if hypre is built without GPU support; refusals of a
  missing value and of the size of the pool of hypre with --execution cpu.
  CPU suite 198/198, GPU variants 20/20.
